WEBVTT

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:02.350
We’re resuming the hunt for Numbers.

00:00:02.350 --> 00:00:06.110
Yuma Tsukumo was wearing
this strange pendant.

00:00:07.570 --> 00:00:14.660
I didn’t expect the Number
Hunter Kaito to attack me again.

00:00:17.740 --> 00:00:22.080
Shark tried to protect the King’s
Key, but Kaito took his soul.

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:26.500
Even worse, he stole the King’s Key.

00:00:27.150 --> 00:00:30.340
Astral is inside the King’s Key.

00:00:30.550 --> 00:00:34.250
Just wait, Astral! I’ll save you!

00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:39.680
Shark!

00:00:39.680 --> 00:00:42.150
Pull yourself together, Shark!

00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:50.230
What are the results?

00:00:50.230 --> 00:00:52.740
I’m currently analyzing it.

00:01:00.990 --> 00:01:04.960
Master Kaito, why are you
obsessing about this pendant?

00:01:04.960 --> 00:01:06.920
I want to know the truth.

00:01:12.090 --> 00:01:15.220
Dr. Faker isn’t telling
the whole story.

00:01:15.220 --> 00:01:17.590
Therefore, I’ll
uncover it on my own.

00:01:17.590 --> 00:01:21.760
Master Kaito, are you
circumventing Dr. Faker?

00:01:21.760 --> 00:01:24.020
Stay quiet and do your analysis!

00:01:24.020 --> 00:01:25.980
Understood!

00:01:33.810 --> 00:01:37.990
The doctor says that there’s
nothing wrong with his body.

00:01:37.990 --> 00:01:40.520
Then why doesn’t he
regain his senses?

00:01:40.520 --> 00:01:42.700
To summarize, it’s because...

00:01:42.700 --> 00:01:44.940
He’s unconscious.

00:01:44.940 --> 00:01:46.660
No.

00:01:46.660 --> 00:01:49.130
Shark had his soul taken.

00:01:52.300 --> 00:01:54.260
Soul taken?

00:01:54.260 --> 00:01:57.260
Yuma, what do you mean?

00:01:57.260 --> 00:02:00.620
If you lose in a duel
against Kaito,

00:02:00.620 --> 00:02:03.930
he takes your soul
along with your Number Cards!

00:02:08.350 --> 00:02:11.810
He also took my King’s Key.

00:02:15.320 --> 00:02:19.740
Astral is inside it!

00:02:19.740 --> 00:02:20.970
Astral?

00:02:20.970 --> 00:02:22.040
Yeah.

00:02:22.040 --> 00:02:24.490
There’s a special area
inside the King’s Key.

00:02:24.490 --> 00:02:28.460
He’s always there when
he’s not by my side.

00:02:28.460 --> 00:02:31.050
To summarize, Kaito
took Shark’s soul

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:33.870
and the King’s Key
with Astral inside?

00:02:33.870 --> 00:02:35.700
Let’s find Kaito!

00:02:35.700 --> 00:02:37.380
But how?

00:02:37.380 --> 00:02:41.210
Since he took the key, he’ll
most likely examine it.

00:02:41.210 --> 00:02:44.540
To summarize, he’ll analyze
it with a computer.

00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:49.560
Yuma, there may be a way
to find the King’s Key!

00:02:49.560 --> 00:02:51.850
No way!

00:02:51.850 --> 00:02:52.720
What is it?

00:02:52.720 --> 00:02:57.070
It’s unbelievable! There’s
a different gravitational field inside it!

00:02:57.070 --> 00:02:59.530
Gravitational field?
What do you mean?

00:03:00.050 --> 00:03:05.060
The inside of this pendant
connects to a different dimension.

00:03:05.540 --> 00:03:08.430
Is it the Astral World?

00:03:08.430 --> 00:03:09.960
Can you open the entrance?

00:03:09.960 --> 00:03:11.480
Understood!

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:16.740
Spread a computer virus?

00:03:16.740 --> 00:03:18.670
It’s the only way!

00:03:18.670 --> 00:03:23.870
The guy who stole Yuma’s King’s Key
will examine it by using a computer.

00:03:23.870 --> 00:03:27.710
So you want to find it by
hacking the information.

00:03:27.710 --> 00:03:30.310
It’ll be easy with your
computer skills, teacher!

00:03:30.310 --> 00:03:31.800
But...

00:03:31.800 --> 00:03:33.770
Please, teacher!

00:03:33.770 --> 00:03:37.280
If you don’t, neither Shark
nor Astral will come back!

00:03:38.230 --> 00:03:40.530
Teacher, a moment of your time.

00:03:43.950 --> 00:03:46.890
You’ll do it, right?

00:03:46.890 --> 00:03:51.040
If you don’t, I’ll tell everyone
that you spread the Crashbug virus.

00:03:51.040 --> 00:03:52.080
What?

00:03:52.080 --> 00:03:56.040
You created chaos
throughout the city.

00:03:56.590 --> 00:03:58.460
You’re...

00:04:04.210 --> 00:04:05.850
He’ll do it!

00:04:05.850 --> 00:04:06.970
All right!

00:04:06.970 --> 00:04:10.100
Teacher, hurry up!

00:04:10.100 --> 00:04:10.880
Hey!

00:04:10.880 --> 00:04:12.190
Yuma!

00:04:12.190 --> 00:04:13.640
Kotori?

00:04:13.640 --> 00:04:17.640
If you find Kaito’s location,
I know you’re going there.

00:04:17.640 --> 00:04:20.020
And you’re going to duel him.

00:04:20.020 --> 00:04:21.110
Kotori...

00:04:21.110 --> 00:04:25.460
I know that you have to
rescue Astral and Shark.

00:04:25.460 --> 00:04:26.710
But...

00:04:27.910 --> 00:04:30.290
It’ll be fine. Don’t worry.

00:04:30.290 --> 00:04:33.290
I won’t lose against Kaito!

00:04:35.710 --> 00:04:40.710
Class representative, is it safe
to spread a computer virus?

00:04:40.710 --> 00:04:41.920
Of course!

00:04:41.920 --> 00:04:44.680
Even though it’s called a virus,
it’s not an evil program.

00:04:44.680 --> 00:04:50.640
It’s a program that searches network
data regarding the King’s Key.

00:04:50.640 --> 00:04:56.600
Our teacher’s virus will
definitely find Yuma’s King’s Key.

00:04:56.600 --> 00:04:57.800
Bug!

00:04:57.800 --> 00:04:59.940
Crashbug!

00:04:59.940 --> 00:05:04.490
Why does the teacher’s computer
virus look like Crashbug?

00:05:05.110 --> 00:05:07.860
Is there a connection
with the Crashbug virus?

00:05:07.860 --> 00:05:11.950
There’s no way our teacher
was involved! Right?

00:05:15.250 --> 00:05:18.280
I reformatted the virus.

00:05:18.280 --> 00:05:19.960
Go, Crashbug!

00:05:29.050 --> 00:05:31.380
I’m counting on you, Crashbug!

00:05:35.480 --> 00:05:38.730
Whether it’s rain, wind,
blizzard or the scorching sun

00:05:38.730 --> 00:05:41.860
They give color to each day;
Will and love keep me from losing heart

00:05:41.860 --> 00:05:44.780
Your kindness was harsh;
I learned frustration when we clashed

00:05:44.780 --> 00:05:49.030
Freedom begins by accepting differences;
Dance and create the universe

00:05:51.160 --> 00:05:56.410
In truth, I was sad
until I met you

00:05:57.330 --> 00:06:02.950
I lied, thinking it was
easier to be alone

00:06:02.950 --> 00:06:09.510
Even though we don’t like
the same books or hobbies

00:06:09.510 --> 00:06:13.390
You’re the only one
who agreed with me

00:06:13.390 --> 00:06:16.520
Joy and sadness and anger
and do re mi fa so la ti do

00:06:16.520 --> 00:06:18.380
There’s no harmony and scenario
without differences

00:06:19.110 --> 00:06:21.690
Everyone is not the same

00:06:22.520 --> 00:06:26.610
That’s the reason for living

00:06:26.610 --> 00:06:31.870
Even if the sounds
are dissonant at times

00:06:31.870 --> 00:06:37.290
That’s why I never give up;
I believe my strength will get me through

00:06:38.330 --> 00:06:40.540
I travel to
the edge of the world

00:06:41.180 --> 00:06:45.000
The sights I see
with you are the truth

00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:47.840
Whether it’s rain, wind,
blizzard or the scorching sun

00:06:47.840 --> 00:06:51.090
They give color to each day;
Will and love keep me from losing heart

00:06:51.390 --> 00:06:54.470
Your kindness was harsh;
I learned frustration when we clashed

00:06:54.470 --> 00:06:58.140
Freedom begins by accepting differences;
Dance and create the universe

00:07:06.100 --> 00:07:09.240
It’s no good. There’s no response.

00:07:09.240 --> 00:07:15.790
\hDuel of Destiny! Astral vs Kaito\h

00:07:09.240 --> 00:07:15.790
Number 23:

00:07:09.240 --> 00:07:13.440
It doesn’t respond to Earth substances.

00:07:13.440 --> 00:07:15.790
Try the Baria Light.

00:07:15.790 --> 00:07:17.500
Baria Light.

00:07:18.600 --> 00:07:22.500
We acquired it from the Barian World.

00:07:22.500 --> 00:07:26.270
Nice idea, Master Kaito!

00:07:26.270 --> 00:07:28.710
But where’s the Baria Light?

00:07:28.710 --> 00:07:29.670
Use yours.

00:07:31.000 --> 00:07:34.500
I can’t function without its energy!

00:07:34.500 --> 00:07:37.210
A small amount won’t be a problem.
Hurry up.

00:07:37.210 --> 00:07:38.720
But...

00:07:39.190 --> 00:07:41.190
Understood...

00:07:46.800 --> 00:07:50.090
My precious energy...

00:07:50.090 --> 00:07:52.860
I’ll just put in a little bit.

00:07:58.320 --> 00:08:01.800
I’ll bring the Baria Light
near the King’s Key.

00:08:05.560 --> 00:08:07.780
The pendant is resonating.

00:08:11.920 --> 00:08:15.230
The space mass is
currently increasing.

00:08:15.230 --> 00:08:17.380
The gravitational force
is also changing.

00:08:17.380 --> 00:08:19.050
Can it be?

00:08:22.690 --> 00:08:25.650
The door opened.

00:08:26.640 --> 00:08:29.780
This is the entrance
to the Astral World.

00:08:31.610 --> 00:08:32.860
Master Kaito.

00:08:37.370 --> 00:08:39.510
Master Kaito!

00:08:49.130 --> 00:08:51.560
What is this place?

00:09:00.060 --> 00:09:02.310
Where is it?

00:09:08.350 --> 00:09:09.940
Bug!

00:09:09.940 --> 00:09:11.610
Crashbug!

00:09:11.610 --> 00:09:13.470
There’s a response!

00:09:13.470 --> 00:09:14.820
What’s this?

00:09:14.820 --> 00:09:19.050
It’s a Heartland
warehouse at Pier 4.

00:09:19.050 --> 00:09:20.790
The King’s Key is there.

00:09:20.790 --> 00:09:22.500
Yuma!

00:09:22.500 --> 00:09:24.210
I found you.

00:09:27.170 --> 00:09:30.880
You’re the envoy from the Astral World.

00:09:30.880 --> 00:09:33.830
So it was you, Kaito.

00:09:33.830 --> 00:09:35.740
How do you know my name?

00:09:35.740 --> 00:09:38.680
I fought you once before.

00:09:38.680 --> 00:09:39.430
Me?

00:09:42.690 --> 00:09:44.140
That Number...

00:09:48.060 --> 00:09:49.590
I see.

00:09:49.590 --> 00:09:53.230
The original Number has
possessed Yuma Tsukumo.

00:09:53.230 --> 00:09:56.460
You stole the King’s Key from Yuma.

00:09:56.460 --> 00:09:58.890
So it’s called the King’s Key.

00:09:58.890 --> 00:10:01.080
Why are you searching for Numbers?

00:10:01.080 --> 00:10:02.680
Why are you?

00:10:02.680 --> 00:10:05.450
Numbers are pieces of my memories.

00:10:05.450 --> 00:10:08.120
What? Your memories?

00:10:08.120 --> 00:10:12.190
Yes. That’s why I’m
retrieving the Numbers.

00:10:12.190 --> 00:10:14.140
But why are you?

00:10:14.910 --> 00:10:19.800
To learn the secrets of the Astral World,
the Numbers and the Barian World.

00:10:19.800 --> 00:10:21.260
Barian?

00:10:21.260 --> 00:10:26.280
I must retrieve all the
Numbers and find the answers.

00:10:26.280 --> 00:10:30.190
Hand over all your Numbers.

00:10:30.190 --> 00:10:33.840
We’re both going to
wager all our Numbers?

00:10:34.650 --> 00:10:36.680
Destiny has opened the door.

00:10:36.680 --> 00:10:38.360
Let’s duel.

00:10:41.340 --> 00:10:43.830
Just wait, Astral!

00:10:43.830 --> 00:10:46.610
Duel mode! Photon change!

00:11:00.470 --> 00:11:05.180
I’ll hunt all your Numbers!

00:11:05.180 --> 00:11:08.720
Kaito, it’s finally
time for us to battle.

00:11:08.720 --> 00:11:10.900
I won’t run or hide.

00:11:15.360 --> 00:11:16.320
Here I go!

00:11:16.320 --> 00:11:17.900
Duel!

00:11:27.850 --> 00:11:28.870
What’s wrong?

00:11:31.720 --> 00:11:33.540
Is Astral...

00:11:33.540 --> 00:11:36.380
My turn! I draw!

00:11:36.380 --> 00:11:39.890
I set a monster in defense position!

00:11:41.220 --> 00:11:44.600
Then I set a card and end my turn!

00:11:44.600 --> 00:11:47.530
I set Gogogo Golem.

00:11:47.530 --> 00:11:52.640
When it’s in defense position, it won’t be destroyed in battle once per turn.

00:11:52.640 --> 00:11:58.070
The other card I set was the
trap card Battle Break.

00:11:58.070 --> 00:12:04.070
If he attacks, this card destroys
his monster and ends the battle.

00:12:04.070 --> 00:12:08.040
What will you do about
this setup, Kaito?

00:12:08.040 --> 00:12:11.110
My turn! I draw!

00:12:11.530 --> 00:12:14.540
First, I’ll seal away your set card!

00:12:15.250 --> 00:12:17.980
I summon Reverse Buster.

00:12:26.220 --> 00:12:31.430
When Reverse Buster battles, your
spell and trap cards are sealed.

00:12:33.340 --> 00:12:35.370
Go, Reverse Buster!

00:12:35.370 --> 00:12:37.360
Attack the set monster
in defense position!

00:12:45.240 --> 00:12:47.950
Just like I thought,
it’s Gogogo Golem.

00:12:47.950 --> 00:12:50.550
Reverse Buster’s effect activates!

00:12:50.550 --> 00:12:51.830
What?

00:12:51.830 --> 00:12:55.070
When Reverse Buster battles a set
monster in defense position,

00:12:55.070 --> 00:12:58.670
your monster is destroyed
without calculating damage.

00:12:59.210 --> 00:13:01.670
Gogogo Golem’s effect
to avoid destruction

00:13:01.670 --> 00:13:04.730
only activates during battle.

00:13:04.730 --> 00:13:07.930
You can’t use it against
a destruction effect!

00:13:10.640 --> 00:13:13.850
When Reverse Buster uses its
effect to destroy a set

00:13:13.850 --> 00:13:17.810
monster in defense position,
it gains 500 ATK.

00:13:17.810 --> 00:13:20.570
2000 ATK!

00:13:21.480 --> 00:13:25.620
To summon his ace monster,
Galaxy-Eyes Photon Dragon,

00:13:25.620 --> 00:13:29.660
Kaito has to tribute two monsters
with at least 2000 ATK.

00:13:29.910 --> 00:13:34.580
Is he preparing to summon
Galaxy-Eyes by using this monster?

00:13:35.410 --> 00:13:40.340
He also managed to destroyed my
defense with only one monster.

00:13:40.340 --> 00:13:44.340
I set one card and end my turn.

00:13:44.340 --> 00:13:46.890
Incredible, Kaito.

00:13:46.890 --> 00:13:51.010
Your dueling exceeds
my expectations.

00:13:51.010 --> 00:13:52.350
What an honor.

00:13:52.350 --> 00:13:56.020
But you can’t flatter me
into lowering my guard.

00:13:56.020 --> 00:13:58.060
That’s not my intention.

00:13:58.060 --> 00:14:01.880
You’re the strongest duelist I know.

00:14:01.880 --> 00:14:04.690
You put your soul into dueling.

00:14:04.690 --> 00:14:06.700
What makes you do that?

00:14:07.540 --> 00:14:10.540
You’re so confident that you
had time to observe me.

00:14:10.540 --> 00:14:15.840
It’s because my burden
is greater than yours.

00:14:15.840 --> 00:14:20.130
It must be why you’re
gathering Numbers.

00:14:20.130 --> 00:14:23.490
I don’t need to tell you because
I’m going to eliminate you!

00:14:23.490 --> 00:14:25.630
I see. That’s too bad.

00:14:25.630 --> 00:14:30.390
You’re charming me because you
and Yuma share the same traits.

00:14:30.390 --> 00:14:31.850
What?

00:14:31.850 --> 00:14:32.670
That’s right.

00:14:32.670 --> 00:14:37.560
I tried to possess Yuma,
so I can feel his heart.

00:14:38.290 --> 00:14:40.520
In the depths of
Yuma’s heart,

00:14:40.520 --> 00:14:42.650
he feels sadness for
losing his parents.

00:14:42.650 --> 00:14:45.710
Despite his sadness,
he leads his life

00:14:45.710 --> 00:14:48.900
trusting what his
parents taught him.

00:14:48.900 --> 00:14:51.660
I’m like him?

00:14:51.660 --> 00:14:52.870
That’s right.

00:14:52.870 --> 00:14:54.080
Whatever!

00:14:54.080 --> 00:14:57.380
I don’t have parents!
I only have Haruto!

00:14:57.380 --> 00:14:58.520
Haruto?

00:14:58.520 --> 00:15:00.340
Enough talk!

00:15:00.340 --> 00:15:03.750
Continue the duel! It’s your turn!

00:15:04.350 --> 00:15:07.760
My turn! I draw!

00:15:07.760 --> 00:15:10.880
I summon Gogogo Giant!

00:15:15.460 --> 00:15:18.670
When this card is summoned,
I can Special Summon

00:15:18.670 --> 00:15:21.230
Gogogo Golem from my graveyard
in defense position!

00:15:25.190 --> 00:15:29.900
When I use this effect, Gogogo Giant
switches to defense position.

00:15:35.370 --> 00:15:38.830
He now has two Level 4
monsters on his field.

00:15:39.790 --> 00:15:42.870
Is he bringing out
Utopia, his Number?

00:15:43.320 --> 00:15:45.950
The problem is Kaito’s set card.

00:15:45.950 --> 00:15:50.050
Is it a trap that’s
waiting for my Number?

00:15:52.680 --> 00:15:56.930
I activate the Continuous Spell
Double Defender from my hand!

00:15:58.720 --> 00:16:03.060
When there are two monsters
in face-up defense position on my field,

00:16:03.060 --> 00:16:07.640
it negates your monster’s attack
once per turn.

00:16:09.150 --> 00:16:12.640
I set one card and end my turn!

00:16:13.110 --> 00:16:17.760
I thought you would
summon your ace Utopia.

00:16:17.760 --> 00:16:20.610
But if you summon Utopia,
you’ll lose Gogogo Golem

00:16:20.610 --> 00:16:23.460
and Gogogo Giant that are
in defense position.

00:16:23.460 --> 00:16:26.840
Even with Utopia’s effect,
you have less defense.

00:16:26.840 --> 00:16:31.310
You’re using those two set cards
to stop my attack, right?

00:16:32.090 --> 00:16:34.480
Are you being careful
about my set card?

00:16:34.480 --> 00:16:37.600
Or are you afraid of Galaxy-Eyes?

00:16:41.230 --> 00:16:43.850
My turn! I draw!

00:16:44.440 --> 00:16:48.270
I activate the spell
card Photon Hurricane!

00:16:48.270 --> 00:16:51.610
For every card in my hand,

00:16:51.610 --> 00:16:54.700
a spell or trap card on your field
returns to your hand.

00:16:54.700 --> 00:16:59.160
Therefore, all your set
cards return to your hand.

00:16:59.160 --> 00:17:00.660
What?

00:17:00.660 --> 00:17:01.510
That’s right.

00:17:01.510 --> 00:17:03.870
The set card that you
were scared of...

00:17:03.870 --> 00:17:06.080
Was an ordinary spell card.

00:17:06.080 --> 00:17:07.210
That’s right.

00:17:07.210 --> 00:17:10.300
It’s not a card that could’ve
countered your attack.

00:17:10.300 --> 00:17:15.050
If you attacked last turn,
you would be in a different situation.

00:17:15.050 --> 00:17:19.720
I tribute Reverse Buster to
Tribute Summon Photon Leo!

00:17:24.390 --> 00:17:26.650
Photon Leo’s effect activates!

00:17:29.980 --> 00:17:31.520
Howling Blow!

00:17:34.200 --> 00:17:37.990
When this card is summoned,
your hand returns to your deck,

00:17:37.990 --> 00:17:41.700
and then you draw
the same number of cards.

00:17:43.230 --> 00:17:46.580
Draw a new hand!

00:17:46.580 --> 00:17:48.040
Damn!

00:17:48.040 --> 00:17:51.720
Your entire strategy is
back to the beginning.

00:17:52.750 --> 00:17:54.560
I’m disappointed.

00:17:54.560 --> 00:17:57.220
Your current strategy
only focuses on defense.

00:17:57.220 --> 00:17:59.720
You’re too scared.

00:18:14.480 --> 00:18:15.580
Open!

00:18:15.580 --> 00:18:17.250
Open!

00:18:18.450 --> 00:18:20.080
Open!

00:18:20.080 --> 00:18:22.160
Yuma, your deck is glowing again.

00:18:25.370 --> 00:18:27.530
Astral is battling.

00:18:27.530 --> 00:18:29.330
Astral is in trouble!

00:18:29.330 --> 00:18:30.500
What do you mean?

00:18:30.500 --> 00:18:33.960
I know that he’s battling!

00:18:33.960 --> 00:18:35.610
Astral against who?

00:18:35.610 --> 00:18:37.670
The Number Hunter?

00:18:37.670 --> 00:18:41.470
Damn! Open!

00:18:41.470 --> 00:18:46.200
From my hand, I equip the Equip
Spell Photon Spear on Photon Leo!

00:18:52.860 --> 00:18:55.310
When the monster equipped
with Photon Spear

00:18:55.310 --> 00:18:57.520
attacks a monster in
defense position...

00:18:57.520 --> 00:19:03.200
...if its ATK are greater than your DEF, the difference is dealt as damage.

00:19:03.200 --> 00:19:06.160
Photon Leo, attack Gogogo Giant!

00:19:06.160 --> 00:19:08.940
Silver Fang!

00:19:19.680 --> 00:19:23.140
I didn’t know I was scared.

00:19:23.140 --> 00:19:25.600
I can’t beat Kaito that way.

00:19:26.110 --> 00:19:30.350
I forgot what was important.

00:19:35.360 --> 00:19:36.790
It’s no good.

00:19:37.530 --> 00:19:40.850
Damn! After I’ve come this far!

00:19:41.530 --> 00:19:45.670
In the end, I can’t
save Astral or Shark?

00:19:52.540 --> 00:19:54.070
Yuma...

00:19:58.240 --> 00:19:59.550
Yuma!

00:20:05.260 --> 00:20:07.820
Yuma, pull yourself together!

00:20:07.820 --> 00:20:10.020
You’re not allowed to fall apart!

00:20:10.020 --> 00:20:11.420
Kotori...

00:20:14.920 --> 00:20:17.020
You’re right.

00:20:17.940 --> 00:20:22.020
I’m the only one who
can save Astral.

00:20:25.410 --> 00:20:26.650
Open!

00:20:27.950 --> 00:20:31.160
Open!

00:20:33.080 --> 00:20:36.190
Open!

00:20:45.640 --> 00:20:48.600
The door opened?

00:20:52.310 --> 00:20:55.340
I sent a virus into
its security system.

00:20:55.340 --> 00:20:57.270
This is your chance to get inside!

00:20:57.270 --> 00:20:59.250
You’re the best, Mr. Ukyo!

00:20:59.250 --> 00:21:01.280
Let’s go, everyone!

00:21:03.730 --> 00:21:06.700
Master Kaito!

00:21:06.700 --> 00:21:08.950
Are you okay?

00:21:08.950 --> 00:21:12.210
If you’re okay, please answer.

00:21:14.500 --> 00:21:18.460
Crashbug!

00:21:22.300 --> 00:21:23.130
What’s going on?

00:21:26.550 --> 00:21:28.800
Oh my!

00:21:30.010 --> 00:21:31.010
What?

00:21:31.010 --> 00:21:34.230
Intruders discovered in Area 3.

00:21:34.840 --> 00:21:38.190
Who are they? What should I do?

00:21:38.190 --> 00:21:42.900
If I fail, he’ll really
turn me into scrap!

00:21:42.900 --> 00:21:45.360
Your skills aren’t bad.

00:21:45.360 --> 00:21:47.590
However, you should
give up on this duel.

00:21:47.590 --> 00:21:50.830
Your heart is too weak to beat me.

00:21:50.830 --> 00:21:52.890
No, I won’t give up.

00:21:52.890 --> 00:21:56.210
It’s true that I would’ve
given up in the past.

00:21:58.960 --> 00:22:01.670
But now, I won’t give up!

00:22:03.130 --> 00:22:07.380
Because a dear friend
taught me about kattobing!

00:22:13.240 --> 00:22:15.580
Let’s start the duel!

00:22:15.580 --> 00:22:17.580
This week’s quiz:

00:22:17.580 --> 00:22:20.110
When an Xyz Monster
activates its effect,

00:22:20.110 --> 00:22:22.650
where do you send
its Overlay Unit?

00:22:22.650 --> 00:22:24.900
To the graveyard or the deck?

00:22:30.600 --> 00:22:35.200
Today’s test is hard;
Can’t avoid pleasure and temptation

00:22:35.200 --> 00:22:39.960
I want to go home and watch TV;
Recent cartoons are entertaining

00:22:49.890 --> 00:22:54.800
Anyway, tests are hard;
Language, math and English are especially hard

00:22:54.800 --> 00:22:59.560
Average scores in science and social studies;
I’m only good at P.E.

00:22:59.560 --> 00:23:02.660
(Wait, Baby!) The expected

00:23:02.660 --> 00:23:04.860
(What’s that, Baby!) Answers

00:23:04.860 --> 00:23:07.660
(Wait a sec, Baby!) Remember them

00:23:07.660 --> 00:23:08.900
(What are we!? Baby!) For who

00:23:08.900 --> 00:23:13.960
Let’s say I wrote
the correct answers on that sheet

00:23:13.960 --> 00:23:18.160
Will that change the future a year
or a decade from now?

00:23:19.160 --> 00:23:23.900
The world I drew
at the edge of dreams

00:23:23.900 --> 00:23:28.170
Someday I’ll race in the sky

00:23:28.660 --> 00:23:33.390
Nobody can threaten my heart

00:23:33.390 --> 00:23:37.470
Nothing is correct!

00:23:41.100 --> 00:23:42.800
Astral is battling!

00:23:42.800 --> 00:23:44.770
I have to go there right away!

00:23:44.770 --> 00:23:47.570
Am I unable to beat him?

00:23:47.570 --> 00:23:48.360
Come with me!

00:23:48.360 --> 00:23:50.150
But Yuma is still inside!

00:23:50.670 --> 00:23:52.780
It’s ZEXAL.

00:23:52.780 --> 00:23:56.080
The miraculous power that
will save my planet.

00:23:56.080 --> 00:23:58.850
I’ll acquire it, no matter what
sacrifices I have to make!

00:23:58.850 --> 00:24:02.460
Yuma and I build the
Overlay Network!

00:24:02.460 --> 00:24:10.010
\h\hXyz Summon of Souls! ZEXAL\h\h

00:24:02.460 --> 00:24:06.710
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ZEXAL:
“Xyz Summon of Souls! ZEXAL”

00:24:06.710 --> 00:24:10.010
I’m kattobing!

00:24:12.510 --> 00:24:15.200
The answer is... the graveyard!

00:24:15.680 --> 00:24:19.400
By sending Overlay Units
to the graveyard,

00:24:19.400 --> 00:24:23.120
you can activate Xyz
Monsters’ effects!
